            {
              "id": "CVE-2022-41720-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2022-41720 high vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "On Windows, restricted files can be accessed via os.DirFS and http.Dir. The os.DirFS function and http.Dir type provide access to a tree of files rooted at a given directory. These functions permit access to Windows device files under that root. For example, os.DirFS(\"C:/tmp\").Open(\"COM1\") opens the COM1 device. Both os.DirFS and http.Dir only provide read-only filesystem access. In addition, on Windows, an os.DirFS for the directory (the root of the current drive) can permit a maliciously crafted path to escape from the drive and access any path on the system. With fix applied, the behavior of os.DirFS(\"\") has changed. Previously, an empty root was treated equivalently to \"/\", so os.DirFS(\"\").Open(\"tmp\") would open the path \"/tmp\". This now returns an error."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2022-41720\nSeverity: high\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.14.4\nFix Version: 1.18.9,1.19.4\nType: go-module\nLocation: /source/taos-internal/tests/pytest/go/httpTest_query_st_in\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2022-41720](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-41720)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2022-41720**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | stdlib  | go1.14.4  | 1.18.9,1.19.4  | go-module  | /source/taos-internal/tests/pytest/go/httpTest_query_st_in  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2022-41720](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-41720)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.14.4"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-61726-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-61726 high vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The net/url package does not set a limit on the number of query parameters in a query. While the maximum size of query parameters in URLs is generally limited by the maximum request header size, the net/http.Request.ParseForm method can parse large URL-encoded forms. Parsing a large form containing many unique query parameters can cause excessive memory consumption."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
